-- title:
--   Injectivity of Sylow restriction for pronilpotent groups
-- statement:
--   Let $J$ be a pronilpotent profinite group acting continuously by automorphisms on a finite discrete $p$-group $N$, where $p$ is prime. Let $P$ be a Sylow pro-$p$ subgroup of $J$, and let $\varphi,\psi:J\to N$ be continuous nonabelian cocycles. If their restrictions to $P$ are cohomologous, then
--
--   $$[\varphi|_P]=[\psi|_P]\quad\Longrightarrow\quad[\varphi]=[\psi]\text{ in }H^1(J,N).$$
--
--   Cohomology means that $\psi(x)=n^{-1}\varphi(x)(x\cdot n)$ for one fixed $n\in N$ throughout the domain. This is the injectivity part of Sylow restriction for pronilpotent acting groups.
-- source:
--   Michael C. Burkhart, Local conjugacy in prosolvable groups, https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.37678; supporting formalization lemma, LocalConjugacy/PronilpotentZorn.lean, lines 62–93; source SHA-256 513161a3df0f10b55069b0bafeda3c91abd1bb6268dcd7b33b0a1ec0764512d3.

